omakasui-nvim (1:0.0.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Move setup-nvim under usr/lib/omakasui-nvim/ and install it through
    debian/omakasui-nvim.install.
  * Add -y/--yes to skip the confirmation and --no-backup to
    delete the existing config instead of backing it up in setup-nvim.
  * Ignore debian/omakasui-nvim/ and the commit-named starter directory.

 -- Luca Pattocchio <info@lucapattocchio.dev>  Tue, 01 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0200

omakasui-nvim (1:0.0.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Pin the LazyVim starter by commit and verify its checksum.
  * Commit lazy-lock.json and restore from it instead of syncing to HEAD
  * Fail the build when the plugin restore does not produce a usable cache, instead of shipping an empty one.
  * Ship the payload once in omakasui-nvim.
  * setup-nvim: derive the project from the invoked name, use id -un instead
    of $USER, declare xdg-utils, and state in the prompt that plugin data, state and cache are deleted without a backup.

 -- Luca Pattocchio <info@lucapattocchio.dev>  Mon, 17 Aug 2026 00:25:00 +0200

